  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 850 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nBy the start of the long term, ridging will be centered over the \nTN Valley. This will be paired with high pressure over the eastern\nCONUS at the surface. The high pressure will work to keep rain \nchances low and set temps on a warming trend. Highs look to warm \nfrom the low 90s back to the high 90s by the end of the week. \nSurface high pressure will induce weak ESE flow which will \ngradually return dew points to the 70s. While we will have to keep\nand eye on trends, models currently keep dew points in the low \n70s which will work in our favor to keep heat indices below Heat \nAdvisory criteria (105F). Under ESE flow, dew points look highest \nin NE AL. As such, low chances (20% or less) for terrain enhanced\nshowers are forecast each afternoon. Without any widespread \nforcing for clouds and rain, heat will be our primary concern \nthrough the long term forecast. Make sure to check back for \nupdates and continue to practice proper heat safety.",
